[size=6][b]Hardcore Space Realism for SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

A [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS]UE4SS[/url] Lua mod: the space counterpart of [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url]. Everything is on by default, automatic, with no keys and no menus. Part of the SpaceBourne 2 realism set.

[b]Status: 0.1.0 (first release).[/b] The ally pod catchers are on by default. The enemy doctrine is in > but [b]off by default[/b] until it has been tested in the game. Smarter allied ships and ship damage that > matters are planned. [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreSpaceRealism/blob/main/DESIGN.md]DESIGN.md[/url] has the research.

[line]
[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[b]Ally pod catchers (0.1.0).[/b] When a ship dies its pilot ejects in a rescue pod. The game lets only you catch it: with your mothership's pod catcher perk or the pod catcher item. With this mod an allied ship that is closer to a free pod than you are, and within range, catches it. The pilot goes to [b]your[/b] captives, exactly as if you had caught it. Nothing is caught when your captive slots are full or when your own mothership perk is on (it already takes every free pod).

[b]Enemy doctrine by tier (0.1.0, off by default).[/b] In the game every enemy fighter and frigate ends its run with a "close pass": it doubles its speed and dives at you. With this on, the low tiers (pirates, and ranks up to LowRank) never do that, so they keep shooting from their normal attack distance, and they turn a little slower (sloppy). Higher ranks of the military factions fly as the game has them. Switch it on with EnemyDoctrine.Enabled = true; it becomes the default once it has been tested.

[i]Planned, not in 0.1.0:[/i]
[list]
[*][b]Smarter allied ships:[/b] pull back when badly damaged, and fleet members that fire at one target.
[*][b]Ship damage that matters:[/b] a ship that has lost hull flies, turns and shoots worse.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Edit HardcoreSpaceRealism/scripts/config.lua, save, restart the game.

[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b]: true (Master switch.)
[*][b]PodCatchers.Enabled[/b]: true (Allied ships catch free pods.)
[*][b]PodCatchers.Range[/b]: 5000 (Metres. An ally this close to a pod, and nearer than you, catches it.)
[*][b]PodCatchers.Interval[/b]: 2.5 (Seconds between checks.)
[*][b]EnemyDoctrine.Enabled[/b]: false (Low-tier enemies skip the close pass and turn slower.)
[*][b]EnemyDoctrine.LowRank[/b]: 1 (Enemy rank up to this is low tier (pirates always are).)
[*][b]EnemyDoctrine.SloppyTurn[/b]: 0.85 (Low-tier turn speed multiplier (1 = unchanged).)
[*][b]EnemyDoctrine.Interval[/b]: 3.0 (Seconds between scans.)
[*][b]Debug[/b]: false (Writes what the mod does to hardcorespacerealism.log.)
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Works with Bigger Armies[/b][/size]

Bigger Armies 0.2.0 had the same pod catchers. If it is installed and on with its PodCatchers setting on, this mod leaves the pods to it and says so once in its log. Bigger Armies 0.2.1 and later no longer has them: update it and this mod takes over.

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[b]A. SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer (recommended)[/b] The [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]installer[/url] installs UE4SS if you don't have it, switches the mods you tick on and keeps them updated.

[b]B. By hand[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install UE4SS 3.0.1 for SpaceBourne 2: put dwmapi.dll, UE4SS.dll and UE4SS-settings.ini in SB2\Binaries\Win64.
[*]Copy the HardcoreSpaceRealism folder to SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods.
[*]Add the line HardcoreSpaceRealism : 1 to Mods\mods.txt (or keep the empty enabled.txt in the mod folder).
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Pod catching uses the game's own CatchByMother call, so the pod flies to the allied ship and the game's own catcher drone animation runs under your ship.
[*]A catch can complete the mission objective "catch a pod" (the game's own rule for any catch).
[*]The pod catchers were tested with scripted allies and pods (in Bigger Armies 0.2.0, same code); a real fleet fight is not tested yet. The enemy doctrine is not tested in the game yet.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

Pure Lua, no game files replaced. Timed work uses gametick.lua (no LoopAsync), the same timer every mod of the set shares, so the mods do not step on each other.

[line]
[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]

The mod looks for free pods (the game tags them FreePod) every few seconds on the game thread. When an ally ship is nearest, it calls the pod's own CatchByMother with that ship, the same call the mothership perk makes. Details: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreSpaceRealism/blob/main/DESIGN.md]DESIGN.md[/url]. Version history: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreSpaceRealism/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]The SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

Separate mods that work alone or in any combination. The [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]) installs the ones you tick and keeps them updated.

[list]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus[/url]): realistic ballistics, wounds and tactical AI. The core of the set.
[*][b]Hardcore Space Realism[/b] (this mod): realism for ships and space combat.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]Silent Ops[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus[/url]): stealth, silent takedowns and suppressors.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-AmmoDiscipline]Ammo Discipline[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/12]Nexus[/url]): carried ammo limits and scavenging, so every magazine counts.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]Gear Without Levels[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus[/url]): use gear above your level, with small handling penalties.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalFirstPerson]Tactical First Person[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/15]Nexus[/url]): first person on foot, weapons held up, aiming down the sights.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]Tactical Engineering[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus[/url]): realistic deployable turrets.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay]Get Out of the Way[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus[/url]): NPCs step aside naturally when you walk through them.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints]Ground Waypoints[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus[/url]): planet waypoints on foot and on the hoverbike.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]Faction Power[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus[/url]): dungeons, strategic sales and missions earn your faction power.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies]Bigger Armies[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/17]Nexus[/url]): twice the general slots for your faction's ground and space forces.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-ClearHUD]Clear HUD[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/16]Nexus[/url]): a reticle you can see and HUD colours of your choice.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]Split Controls[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus[/url]): separate vertical invert for ship and on foot, per device.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]SB2 HOTAS[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus[/url]): HOTAS, rudder pedals, triple screens and head tracking.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics]Squad Tactics[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/18]Nexus[/url]): squad orders on foot: teams, point at a spot and give orders, rescue me.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-UnofficialPatch]Unofficial Patch[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/19]Nexus[/url]): fixes for game bugs, such as squad mates stuck or misplaced in lifts.
[/list]

